; mdx runs the OCaml and shell fences, except those marked skip: installation
; commands, which need the network; `munin` command lines, which name run ids
; generated per run and show output from the reader's store (04-cli.md and
; 05-dashboard.md give them as plain fences); and the Kaun training loop, which
; downloads MNIST.
;
; The guides sample the system through munin.sys, which supports Linux and
; macOS only.

(mdx
 (files *.md)
 (package munin)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{os_type} Win32))
 (preludes prelude.ml)
 (libraries munin munin.sys unix))
